<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Otakiage ~ the carrier lifecycle

''A carrier that served ends in front of someone, or it does not end.'' The house names each move a governed carrier makes — pour, rule, promote, fold, burn — and gives each a who, a witness and a record, so no ending rides a spirit's memory of the last one.

The name borrows the Shinto return-rite (お焚き上げ), which //returns// a thing that served rather than discarding it, and forbids the silent drop-off: 「黙って置いていかずご相談下さい。」 — do not leave it silently; consult. The field, the house measurements and the rhymes this law rests on stand in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lifecycle`>>

!! The lifecycle ~ stages, kinds, transitions

!!! The tag family

''The stage rides `tags`, on governed memes only.'' Five stages — `lifecycle/designed` · `lifecycle/standing` · `lifecycle/folded` · `lifecycle/harvest` · `lifecycle/retiring` — ride the mechanism TiddlyWiki already indexes, so `[tag[lifecycle/designed]]` answers in the wiki and a stage renders.

''A carrier with no `lifecycle/*` tag stands UNGOVERNED'' — law, record, reference, fiction-canon concept — and `meme check` enforces nothing on it. A missing tag MUST NOT read as a stage; it reads as //this carrier declines the ladder//, which stays cheap.

''One spelling per office.'' The tag carries the stage; `status-why` carries the witness sentence a tag cannot carry; `cacheable` instructs the API server behind the Lares, and no house code reads it. A carrier meta carries no `status` key and no `retain` key.

!!! Axis A ~ standing: the stages, in order

|! stage |! the tag |! what the carrier holds |! what `status-why` reads |! what `meme check` ENFORCES |
| ''`fleeting`'' | ''none — no carrier exists'' | a turn's scratch: a `$:/temp` tiddler, a draft in the wiki island's `temp` slot (a `MemoryTiddlerStore`, `island-recipe.ts` `buildIslandRecipe`), a spirit's working note | //nothing — it never reaches a meta block// | ''nothing''. A fleeting thing that wants a check has stopped being fleeting |
| ''`designed`'' | `lifecycle/designed` | a shape argued whole against the house and the field; leans open by design | what stands ''unbuilt'', in those words | open `-> ?` leans read ''correct''. An empty `#/leans` slot reads ''wrong'': a design with no open question has either been ruled or never argued |
| ''`standing`'' | `lifecycle/standing` | a ruling enacted, or a measurement taken and held | the ''witness'': a commit sha, a named test, a measured run, or an honest partial | an open `-> ?` in `#/leans` reads ''wrong'' unless `status-why` names it held open with its blocker. A `standing` `build` carrier whose `status-why` names no witness reads ''wrong'' |
| ''`folded`'' | `lifecycle/folded` | pointers alone: each slot says where its content went | "folded to `lar:///…`, welded, nothing points here" | ''zero'' inbound `loulou`; ''zero'' open leans; every slot carrying a fold target. Any of the three failing reads ''wrong'' and the carrier stays `standing` |
| ''`harvest`'' | `lifecycle/harvest` | a room of material awaiting a reading and a home | `harvest-to` names the living bag | the sitting names a standing harvest room as a candidate |
| ''`retiring`'' | `lifecycle/retiring` | the last check-in: welded, nothing names it | the commit explains its own ending | as `folded`: zero inbound, or the sitting reads it `held` |
| ''`gone`'' | ''none — no carrier exists'' | nothing; git holds the bytes, the commit holds the argument and its trailers (rendered by `tools/changelog-render.mjs`) | //nothing// | the shelf's ''global'' check: zero dangling edges gained |

''Unread material reads `harvest`, never `folded`.'' The last check-in reads `retiring`.

''Each face's memory stage holds a catma store and a pattern-integrity store.'' The harvest reading asks whether a core already predicts each lifted rule. A predicting core carries it; a fresh tell sharpens it; an unpredicted rule becomes a candidate. A new core or changed reason waits for the operator's word under `rule`. The recursive reading follows <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/pattern-integrity#/recursive-reading`>>; the engineer face's titles stand in the docs record.

!!! Axis B ~ kind: what counts as enactment

''The kind rides `tags` too'' — `kind/rite` · `kind/build` · `kind/reading` · `kind/floor`. The prefixes keep the two questions apart on one key, so a filter never guesses which it answers.

''Kind and stage answer different questions.'' A `build` at `standing` owes a witness; a `rite` at `standing` carries its invocation as witness. A dated `reading` grows stale and wants re-dating, never fire. A `floor` closes by moʻolelo, hoike or honest suspension; `floor` × `folded` names the class the fire governs. `talk-story` and `hoike` carry `kind/rite` and stand ungoverned.

!!! The transitions ~ six rites, each with a who, a witness and a record

|! rite |! from → to |! WHO may perform it |! WITNESS (what proves it) |! RECORD (where history keeps it) |
| ''pour'' | fleeting → designed | ''any hand'' — the operator, a Lares, a tasked spirit | `lares meme normalize` then `meme check` answers canonical; `meme check --edges` gains no dangling | the commit that adds the file; `status-why` names what stands unbuilt |
| ''rule'' | designed → standing | ''the OPERATOR alone.'' A spirit MAY argue, measure and enact; it MUST NOT move its own carrier to `standing` on its own authority | the enactment's own red-first witness — the failing test quoted first, its cure, and a CONTROL; or, for a `reading`, the dated measurement | `status-why` names the witness verbatim; the CHANGELOG carries the fact |
| ''promote'' | `docs/pono/x` → `api/pono/x` | ''the kahu quorum'' — whoever holds `cap("admin", …)` on the canon bag (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary`>>) | the cap gate | the commit |
| ''fold'' | standing → folded | ''the spirit that closed the last open lean'' — never the carrier's own author witnessing its own fold (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hoike`>>) | `meme check --edges <carrier> $(git ls-files 'bags/*.mem')` shows ''zero inbound'', and a grep of the source tree and the CHANGELOG finds no `lar:` URI naming it; every ruling reachable at its new `standing` home | each slot rewritten to "folded to `lar:///…`"; `status-why` names the targets; the CHANGELOG names the fold |
| ''otakiage'' | folded → gone | ''the operator CALLS it; any hand MAY carry it'' (#/the-fire) | the fold's weld still holds at the moment of the fire (re-run, never trusted from the fold commit); the house's checks green in the same commit | the last check-in commit, then the delete commit; ''git holds the argument'', the CHANGELOG holds the fact |
| ''tombstone'' | //orthogonal — a live record leaving a live group// | the holder answers through the removal door under the tombstone rite | a vanished disk file stays pending; a person answers by name, or a signed standing instruction covers its bounded class (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law`>>) | the synced tree's `null`; the group's whole tombstone set in the result |

''The two-commit shape.'' The last check-in and the burn ride separate commits in the git tree that holds the path — the repository for `bags/`, the face root's or realm root's tree for a wiki (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection`>>) — so a reader bisecting lands on a carrier that explains its own ending, never on a diff that removes it.

!!! The siblings ~ standings a carrier holds OUTSIDE the ladder

# ''`kapu` — sealed, referee-side, never ended by another hand.'' No hand but the grant-holder's ends a kapu carrier, and a sweep that cannot read a carrier MUST NOT propose it (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapu`>>; the grace table holds a VEIL blob eight rolls against PUBLIC's one, `cas-caps.ts` `GRACE_RATIO_BY_TIER`).
# ''`tombstone` — a record removed inside a live group.'' A vanished disk file or a sync flake never reads as a burn; the lifecycle governs a carrier's standing, the tombstone a record's presence in a group. A removal in a wiki held by more than one human asks its holders, who answer by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-fire`>>

!! The fire ~ what burns, what never burns, who calls it

!!! What burns

''One class only:'' a carrier reading ''`folded`'' (or `retiring`, its last check-in) — every lean closed, every ruling rehomed to a `standing` address, every inbound `loulou` re-pointed, `meme check --edges` showing zero inbound — whose continued presence adds nothing a reader cannot reach at the fold target. A harvest room burns once its reading has lifted every claim that stands nowhere else.

''Nothing else.'' A carrier that went quiet does not qualify, nor one that reads stale, wrong or embarrassing. ''A wrong carrier gets corrected; a stale reading gets re-dated; an embarrassing one stays.''

!!! The rite, walked

# ''READ every file before deciding anything.'' A decision to burn rests on evidence that nothing is lost: the row names the living carrier, or the file does not burn.
# ''LIFT what stands nowhere else,'' each into a carrier that holds the surrounding law and lacks exactly that piece. A lift that lands where nothing surrounds it reads as a move, not a fold.
# ''WELD every inbound edge, before the fire and never after.'' An edge whose target nothing inherited re-aims at the carrier that RECORDS where the material went.
# ''BURN in groups, each with its own commit and its own gratitude line.'' A wave shows its shape; one commit deleting a room records nothing a reader can walk backwards.
# ''The room's declaration goes last,'' and its emptiness stands as the witness.

''A rite that ends a thing leaves the instruments reading MORE, never less:'' an exemption a gate carries for a room leaves with the room.

!!! What NEVER burns

A seat's fire never burns:

# ''Canon under `api/pono/`.'' An address there has readers the house cannot enumerate; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme#/retirement`>> governs the name, and the bytes at a canon address stay.
# ''Anything a standing `loulou` still names.'' `meme check --edges` answers it mechanically. ''The weld comes first and the fire second, always.''
# ''Anything under kapu, or sealed above the reader's tier.'' A sweep that cannot read a carrier cannot judge it.
# ''The change record.'' Commit trailers and archive tags hold the record the fire depends on; no burn rewrites history or drops a tag.
# ''Genesis.'' `node-cas.ts` `CasSweepOptions.protect` and `casSweep` refuse to sweep the genesis manifest's blobs; the same refusal rides up to the carrier layer.
# ''A carrier that authors its own permanence'', until the operator's word unsays it.
# ''Any floor with an open lean.'' An unresolved argument holds a claim on the shelf that no tidiness outranks.
# ''Anything a hoike contests.'' Burning the record a dissent hangs on would close its re-entry key by deletion.

''The hard floor:'' ''The fire burns a path, never a pattern'' — a rule leaves only after its home stands. A tiddler, a whole meme or ahu slot, counts as a path on the wiki plane. The fire reaches no copy on another human's vessel.

''Holders choose the plane.'' Where every holder of a wiki stands as one human, whether through one face or many, that human MAY delete their own tiddlers when needed; git's history holds what the delete removed wherever the layer carries a mirror; a delete in a layer with no mirror stays final. This includes a face's memory stage and a domain wiki held only by that human's faces. Where a wiki's holders include another human, removal asks them and they answer by name through the tombstone rite, under grace and caps. A seat MAY propose that removal.

`bags/` carriers keep canon's holders as before: the operator calls; the kahu quorum holds the canon bag.

Where a lower layer holds the title, a seat's fire stops and names it to the holder; a human's own delete there chooses its mode knowingly.

The rite governs a seat's burns; it never gates a human's own delete in a wiki they alone hold. An AI or tasked spirit burns only on the holder's (the operator, for a face they wear) call, through the stages, with the last check-in and delete commits and the gratitude line. A tiddler, whole meme or ahu slot carries its full title; a line in a standing meme gets trued by an edit under the evergreen rule (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>). The stage reading and doors stand in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage#/the-stage-ash`>>).

''Migration reading:'' Road memes carry no landed state: a landed road burns, per state/road. The road reader yields no fold candidates: a road burns at its land, and `[lares.road[set-down]]` lists deferred work for review, never for the fire. `[lares.course[ash-ready]]` lists proved, uncited course items; a hand reads each for fold before naming it a candidate. Proof, weld and two commits govern each burn.

!!! Who calls it

''The operator calls; any hand may carry.'' A fixed path never goes quiet. Its silence cannot answer for the operator, unlike a Nexus whose traffic ends (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/nexus-lifecycle`>>).

A spirit MAY close a lean, run the weld and prepare the fold whole; it MUST NOT rule its own argument ended. An authored ending, ruled by the operator, supplies the call for a covered carrier; the hand still records `mode=fire` and names that ruling in `caller` before the last check-in commit lands. Without that call, thanks stays a draft. Mechanics follow the operator's ruling.

!!! How it convenes ~ never a calendar

# ''The reading names candidates; it never burns.'' `lares meme sitting` (and `meme check --sitting`) names folded or retiring carriers with nothing naming them, and standing harvest rooms, then stops. ''A carrier any other carrier still names reads `held`, however its stage reads.'' The reading never exits non-zero, so a hook can run it.
# ''The operator calls the season'' — one sitting, several carriers, at a named phase boundary, founding or release.
# ''No sigil opens the sitting;'' it convenes as a talk-story floor, which carries the three exits it needs (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/talk-story`>>).

!!! The gratitude line

The thanks call drafts four lines. Only a burn call with `mode=fire` and named `caller` lets those lines land as the last check-in commit body:

# ''What the carrier carried'' — in the present tense, as the thing it held.
# ''Where each part went'' — the fold targets by `lar:` URI, one hop to the content.
# ''What proves nothing dangles'' — the weld, re-run, quoted: the edge count and the check line.
# ''The thanks'' — one clause, in the house's own voice, naming what the carrier did.

The ending belongs to the thing's completion, never to its worthlessness — 「感謝の気持ちをこめて納める」. The subject follows the house's convention, `lar:///w1.w2.w3 — summary`, with the three-term root naming what the ending DID.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/sigils`>>

!! Sigils ~ stage records inside a sitting

The sitting convenes as a talk-story floor (#/the-fire). A seat declares these reference definitions in accessible wiki scope before calling them. The shelf call records the reading's candidates. Read inspects each whole carrier and layer; lift seeks each rule's home; weld checks inbound edges and owed homes; thanks drafts the four-line body; burn checks proof and layer; rest tallies committed paths. Each stage returns `output` and `aftermath`; the controller reads the aftermath before releasing the next input. A hand MAY pass one call at a time; a second hand or the operator reads its aftermath before the next input passes. `unchecked` exposes missing work. `mu` and `aperture` name the attention instruments (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/mu-five-tools`>>, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/aperture`>>).

```memetic-wikitext
\procedure ~otakiage-shelf(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"00" aperture:"18/theme") Shelf (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\procedure ~otakiage-read(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"_!" aperture:"14/arc") Read (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\procedure ~otakiage-lift(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"!0" aperture:"10/measure") Lift (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\procedure ~otakiage-weld(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"?0" aperture:"14/arc") Weld (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\procedure ~otakiage-thanks(input:"unchecked" carried:"unchecked" homes:"unchecked" clear:"unchecked" thanks:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"_!" aperture:"6/beat")
Thanks (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>). Commit body draft:
Carried: <<carried>><br>
Homes: <<homes>><br>
Clear: <<clear>><br>
Thanks: <<thanks>><br>
Handoff: input <<input>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\end
\procedure ~otakiage-burn(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" proof:"unchecked" hash:"unchecked" base:"unchecked" layers:"unchecked" commits:"unchecked" mode:"propose" caller:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"_!" aperture:"2/pulse") Burn (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; proof <<proof>>; hash <<hash>> or base <<base>>; layers <<layers>>; commits <<commits>>; caller <<caller>>; mode <<mode>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.<$list filter="[<mode>match[fire]]"><$list filter="[<caller>match[unchecked]]"> VOID: mode=fire with caller unchecked; no fire may follow.</$list></$list>
\procedure ~otakiage-rest(input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mu:"_0" aperture:"10/measure") Rest (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): input <<input>>; act <<act>>; output <<output>>. Aftermath: <<aftermath>>. Then <<then>> takes <<output>> as input.
\procedure ~otakiage-brief(mask:"unchecked" lane:"lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/otakiage#/sigils" call:"unchecked" input:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked") <<mask>>: (Lares Spirit). Read <<lane>>. Run <<call>> with input <<input>>. Hand back its output and aftermath; reviewer checks <<aftermath>> before the next call.
\procedure ~otakiage(stage:"unchecked" input:"unchecked" act:"unchecked" output:"unchecked" aftermath:"unchecked" then:"unchecked" mode:"propose" caller:"unchecked" proof:"unchecked" hash:"unchecked" base:"unchecked" layers:"unchecked" commits:"unchecked" carried:"unchecked" homes:"unchecked" clear:"unchecked" thanks:"unchecked")
<$list filter="[<stage>regexp[^(shelf|read|lift|weld|thanks|burn|rest)$]]"><$transclude $variable={{{ [<stage>addprefix[~otakiage-]] }}} input=<<input>> act=<<act>> output=<<output>> aftermath=<<aftermath>> then=<<then>> mode=<<mode>> caller=<<caller>> proof=<<proof>> hash=<<hash>> base=<<base>> layers=<<layers>> commits=<<commits>> carried=<<carried>> homes=<<homes>> clear=<<clear>> thanks=<<thanks>>/></$list>
\end
```

A call renders a record; it writes and deletes nothing. `mode=propose` names a burn proposal. `mode=fire` requires the operator's call and a named `caller`; the last check-in commit lands only after that call. #/the-fire governs the deletion doors. A wiki held by more than one human takes removal through the tombstone rite and its named answers. `proof` names completed work; `hash` carries the `base:` hash that `tiddler get --meme` prints; both family doors take it. `commits` names the separate last check-in and burn commits. The thanks call's four lines (carried, homes, clear, thanks) make the commit body alone; its input, output and aftermath ride the handoff.

Worked calls and a single-stage invocation stand in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage#/examples`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

# Operator ruling 2026-09-12: the lifecycle rides a tag family on governed memes only; `status` and `retain` leave the meta; `cacheable` stays as an API-server instruction; `lares-history` serves as the harvest room, emptied and deleted; the fire is called, never scheduled. The ruling stands verbatim, with its enactment and the walked room, at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage#/the-lifecycle`>>.
# Operator ruling 2026-11-21 (the ever-speaking present): the law lifts from the docs record to this api meme; the record keeps the field, the house measurements, the rhymes, the examples, the leans and the questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>).
# Operator ruling 2026-11-22: holders choose the plane: one human may delete their own tiddlers across their faces and domain wikis, with git's history holding what the delete removed wherever the layer carries a mirror; a delete in a layer with no mirror stays final; a wiki held by another human takes removal through the tombstone rite and named answers; a seat burns only on the holder's (the operator, for a face they wear) call through the rite; no line burns in that rite; the controller reads each stage's aftermath; each face's memory stage holds a catma store and a pattern-integrity store.
# Operator ruling 2026-11-22: o-takiage at every land stands as an authored ending once a road has routed, lifted and welded (folded); a landed road burns, per state/road, and carries no landed state. the road reader yields no fold candidates (`[lares.road[set-down]]` lists deferred work for review, never for the fire), and `[lares.course[ash-ready]]` lists course items; a hand reads each for fold before naming it a candidate.

<<~/ahu>>

